WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:09.700
A female rhesus monkey can no longer drive her pituitary from her hypothalamus.

2
00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:15.420
Researchers give her the missing hormone, GnRH, through a drip.

3
00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:18.080
Given steadily, it fails.

4
00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:22.460
Given as a short burst once an hour, it works.

5
00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:26.020
Why would timing matter more than amount?

6
00:00:26.950 --> 00:00:32.810
In mammals, neurons in the hypothalamus release GnRH into portal vessels.

7
00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:36.350
The vessels carry it to the anterior pituitary.

8
00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:42.110
There, GnRH triggers release of two hormones, LH and FSH.

9
00:00:43.070 --> 00:00:45.390
These gonadotropins act on the gonads.

10
00:00:46.310 --> 00:00:48.210
GnRH is released in pulses.

11
00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:53.830
Together, the three organs form the hypothalamic-pituitary-gonadal axis.

12
00:00:54.700 --> 00:01:03.600
In 1978, Belchetz, Plant, Nakai, Keogh and Knobil studied female rhesus monkeys,

13
00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:06.000
asking whether the pulses matter.

14
00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:11.880
Lesions of the hypothalamus had abolished LH and FSH secretion.

15
00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:14.300
The pituitary was intact.

16
00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:21.180
So the team could replace GnRH by intravenous infusion, either continuously or as

17
00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:26.020
brief infusions once an hour, and read the pituitary's answer in blood samples.

18
00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:29.460
First, a continuous infusion.

19
00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:32.920
The pituitary has the hormone all the time.

20
00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:38.460
If it read only the total amount, the steady drip should have worked at least as

21
00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:40.620
well as pulses. It did not.

22
00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:45.960
Continuous infusion failed to sustain LH and FSH secretion.

23
00:01:46.850 --> 00:01:50.190
Next, brief infusions once an hour.

24
00:01:51.070 --> 00:01:54.750
Hourly pulses restored LH and FSH secretion.

25
00:01:55.850 --> 00:02:00.330
The authors also reported that returning to the hourly schedule brought secretion

26
00:02:00.330 --> 00:02:02.290
back after the steady infusion.

27
00:02:03.233 --> 00:02:09.533
The authors concluded that the pattern of GnRH, not its total amount, controls the

28
00:02:09.533 --> 00:02:13.733
pituitary. The experiment shows pattern reading in this primate.

29
00:02:14.333 --> 00:02:18.993
It does not show where the pulses come from, or what interval is normal in humans.

30
00:02:20.173 --> 00:02:25.093
In mice, switching on kisspeptin neurons in the hypothalamus evoked LH pulses.

31
00:02:25.953 --> 00:02:28.553
Whether they do so in primates is a separate question.

32
00:02:28.553 --> 00:02:32.193
A steady supply is not more GnRH.

33
00:02:32.973 --> 00:02:35.173
Held steady, it turns the pituitary down.
